# The empty-side header's declared-zero exception, on the added-file form
# that carries a zero-declared operand hunk. Both patches add added.c
# through a whole-file @@ -0,0 +1,3 @@ hunk that quotes no pre-image line
# at all, and both patch mod.c, where patch1's own quoted run squashes
# across the lines neither patch quotes and cuts into a partition whose
# new side spends nothing. The zero that added.c's hunk declares never
# reaches the context hunk that partition belongs to, so that hunk's own
# declared new count decides the empty side's start: it is nonzero, and
# the side numbers from the line before the first survivor rather than
# riding the parent's start unchanged.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
exit: 0
